Python is an open-source, general-purpose programming language first released in 1991. It was designed with an emphasis on readability and can be used across a wide range of domains, including software development, automation, data science, machine learning, and artificial intelligence.
Python supports multiple programming paradigms, including object-oriented, procedural, and functional programming.


Python’s role in data science is largely supported by a broad ecosystem of specialized libraries.


NumPy (Numerical Python) provides efficient multidimensional arrays and numerical computing capabilities. It forms part of the computational foundation of the scientific Python ecosystem.
Common uses include:

multidimensional arrays;
matrix operations;
numerical calculations;
linear algebra.




pandas provides data structures and tools for working with tabular data.
Common operations include:

importing data;
filtering observations;
selecting variables;
sorting data;
transforming data;
summarizing and exploring datasets.




Python has a large ecosystem of specialized machine-learning and deep-learning frameworks, including TensorFlow.




